A||||10||MEC91Firebird||85 GT vs. 85 V6 SE||||1||
Z||000000||MEC91Firebird||01-24-2001||11:02 PM||||What is thwe diffrence between these two cars?   All i can tell is that some 85 SE's have V6, that appear to be the same as the 85 GT's?   Whats the deal, how can i tell the two appart? Im looking at an 85 that has the V6, and a luggage rack, but it has the GT nose?   Thanks for the clarification!||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||01-24-2001||11:21 PM||||For the most part (besides the engine diff..some SE's have 6's, some have 4's in 85) the only major diff (that I know of) is the body styling. 85 Se's had the standard coupe body, while the Gts in 85 had the aero package.<BR>You wont find an 85 Se w/ an aero nose and luggage rack (why would you want a luggage rack anyway?), but you can either..1.) replace the front facia w/ an aero one, easy to do and you can find them either in a junk yard or on ebay..or 2.) buy an 8<B>6</B> Se..they have the aero package and you can find some w/luggage racks. Come to think of it, there <I>may</I> be some 85 Gts with luggage racks....hmmm.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MEC91Firebird||01-24-2001||11:29 PM||||Okay, that awnsers my question, there must be 85 GT's with luggague racks, because the one im looking at has the aero package, and a luggague rack, so it was either factory, or it has a new deck lid, thanks for the clarification!||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||01-25-2001||01:50 AM||||Ya know, I don't think I've seen an 85 GT with a rack, but my 86 GT does have one that was factory, so I don't see why it wouldn't have been an option.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||01-25-2001||02:01 AM||||'85 GTs could be had with either a spoiler, a luggage rack or nothing at all.  I have seen all three variations.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||01-25-2001||02:29 PM||||Both my 85SE v-6 4spd and my 85GT auto have factory lugage racks.  Both have the same leather three spoke steering wheel although I think the GT has the GT Fiero emblem in the horn button while the SE has the plain Fiero emblem there.<P>The GT has the aero nose and ground effects on the rocker panels and rear bumper.  The GT also has GT stenciled on the sail panels.  The SE sail panels have SE stenciled on them.<P>GTs have the dual megaphone exhaust tips.  V-6 SEs have dual striaght exhaust tips.<P>The GT has the gold GT Fiero nose emblem while the SE has the silver plain Fiero nose emblem.<P>Other than the plastic body panels and the different exhaust tips both cars are the same.||||reg||1
Z||000006||firstfiero||01-25-2001||06:30 PM||||       My 86 se v6 has the mega phone exhaust tips...are you sure they were only for the 85 gt?   ||||reg||11
Z||000007||JJ-85-2M6||01-25-2001||07:58 PM||||85 se's came with a vinyl steering wheel (leather optional, same as gt/different center) and Y99 suspension (ws6 optional).  All 85 se's came with a luggage rack.  This could be deleted by special order.  They did not come with an aero nose or spoiler, and exhaust pipes were straight black twin tips on the optional v6.  They had the same interior as a GT, save the steering wheel.   <BR>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||01-25-2001||08:48 PM||||Just look at the VIN#.......if it's an '85 GT it will start 1G2PG  while the SE is 1G2PF.<P><BR>firstfiero,<P>They are only talking about the '85 SE......the megaphone tips were on the '84 Indy, '85 GT, '86-'87 SE and '86-'88 GT.  The '85 SE just had the plain tips, like all regular coupes.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||01-26-2001||06:28 PM||||I just  bought WTIIIs '85 GT.  Unfortunately, (sorry WTIII  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )it came from the factory with a luggage rack.  Thanx to mrfiero, it now has the "proper" wing. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
